# Memory Patterns
- All writes go through `policies.rs` (dedupe, confidence, TTL)
- Core memory: tiny, always in prompt (~500 tokens), key-value pairs
- Recall memory: on-demand via memory_search tool, NEVER auto-injected
- Archive: consolidated summaries of old low-value memories
- RAG corpus uses separate indices per source_type (docs, code, configs, convos, runbooks)
- Context manager: Write→Select→Compress→Isolate, compress at 85% capacity
- NEVER inject full MEMORY.md into system prompt (OpenClaw anti-pattern)
